            "explanation": {
                "english": "Hepaticopsida (Liverworts) typically have thalloid or leafy gametophytes with rhizoids. Anthocerotopsida (Hornworts) have a sporophyte with a basal meristematic region. Bryopsida (Mosses) have stomata in their capsule (sporophyte). Pteropsida (Ferns) have true roots, stems, and leaves in the sporophyte generation.",
